What is in the data (privacy)
-----------------------------

Citizen-submitted reports are published only in anonymized, PII-redacted,
aggregate-safe form. The authoritative description of these protections is in
docs/privacy.md; read that document for the full detail. The statements below
describe what the export pipeline in this repository actually implements, and
do not claim anything beyond it:

- Only reports in publishable statuses (validated, corroborated,
  evidence_backed, officially_acknowledged) are exported. Reports that are
  submitted (not yet moderated), rejected, or withdrawn never appear.

- Exports are built from an explicit allowlist of columns. Raw IP addresses,
  device fingerprints, and submission tokens are never stored — only one-way
  SHA-256 digests are — and neither those digests nor any office identifier
  are among the exported columns. They are never selected, not merely
  redacted.

- Free-text descriptions are passed through a deterministic redaction pipeline
  (apps/api/src/utils/redaction.ts) that replaces Aadhaar numbers, Indian
  mobile numbers, email addresses, and 16-digit card numbers with [REDACTED],
  both at ingestion and again at export time.

- Published aggregate statistics are subject to a minimum-volume threshold
  (see docs/methodology.md), so no single report determines a public figure.

This describes the protections the code implements; it is not a warranty.
Citizen reports represent reported experiences and are not automatically
verified findings of wrongdoing (see docs/methodology.md).


